From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bernardo Pereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:59:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] add a mark-only census that discounts external handles

An embedder that pins boa objects in a host-side table makes every
pinned object look rooted to the collector. census() marks the heap as
a collection would but discounts one handle per listed pin, so the
embedder can tell which pinned objects boa itself no longer reaches.
Census::children lists an object's strong edges without marking, so
the embedder can group that unreached graph into components. Nothing
is finalized or freed; marks and root counts are reset afterwards.

A reached script WeakRef roots its target, since script can deref it.
WeakMap and WeakSet entries keep ephemeron semantics: they never yield
their keys, so rooting the keys kept every cycle through a
WeakMap<Element, ...> key alive. An entry of a reached map whose key
stays unmarked is reported as an edge from the key to its value, since
script reaches the value through map.get(key) whenever it reaches the
key.
